[[0,1710818,0,3,0,3,"2017-03-11T01:01:03","Joker68","",[],"","As many as 48 million Twitter accounts aren't people, says study","http://www.cnbc.com/2017/03/10/nearly-48-million-twitter-accounts-could-be-bots-says-study.html","news"],[1,8372232,0,0,0,0,"2017-03-11T01:16:27","EyeoftheChampion","",[],"<p>I. am. a. person.</p>\n<p>Truth.</p>"],[1,8372417,0,5,0,5,"2017-03-11T01:35:04","retprob","",[],"<p>Twitter is a cesspool.1 billion accounts could be artificial and it would'nt matter.</p>"],[1,8372479,0,8,1,7,"2017-03-11T01:40:52","Apathy","",[],"<p>Those are just Hillary's followers. </p>"],[2,8372914,8372479,5,0,5,"2017-03-11T02:29:20","thelastcoldwarrior","",[],"<p>Yep, And they all vote, too.</p>"],[2,8375325,8372479,1,0,1,"2017-03-11T09:29:22","greyhunter4","",[],"<p>Hillbots, roll out! <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/ooOfDsJ.png\">http://i.imgur.com/ooOfDsJ.png</a></p>"],[1,8372510,0,1,0,1,"2017-03-11T01:44:05","GreatWhiteNorth","",[],"<p>It's always been that way. </p>"],[1,8372669,0,27,0,27,"2017-03-11T02:02:40","teatime","",[],"<p>No shit. How do you think a platform can have infinite growth while banning some of the most popular users?</p>"],[2,8373104,8372669,3,0,3,"2017-03-11T02:57:24","BentAxel","",[],"<p>what's crazy; if you look at it economically, each user costs them money in storage and bandwidth. Not incrementally but collectively its gotta have an influence on actual users. </p>"],[1,8372718,0,2,0,2,"2017-03-11T02:08:52","GuyIDisagreeWith","",[],"<p>Can they survive selling advertising to bots?</p>\n<p>Will the oil money continue to cover the tab?</p>"],[1,8372796,0,2,0,2,"2017-03-11T02:17:39","Spaceballs-1","",[],"<p>I am a meat popsicle.</p>"],[1,8372923,0,12,0,12,"2017-03-11T02:30:23","Onlio","",[],"<p>Advertising agencies guarantee that their online ads will get clicks (they won't guarantee sales though). They then program bots to &quot;click&quot; on the ads. They then say &quot;see, we told you this is effective&quot; meanwhile the poor client gets charged a huge amount of money and no actual business.</p>"],[2,8374907,8372923,3,0,3,"2017-03-11T07:46:40","senpaithatignoresyou","",[],"<p>To be fair, if you have to resort to click ads, you are either not in a real industry, or are extremely desperate. </p>"],[1,8373155,0,1,0,1,"2017-03-11T03:06:38","roznak","",[],"<p>You can unmask these bots easily: Ask them if they are connected to the CIA. If they crash or avoid the question then that is a big sign that it is a bot.</p>"],[1,8373194,0,0,0,0,"2017-03-11T03:11:32","dittohead","",[],"<p>48 million? That's it? Just the hamplanets alone at at least 100 million</p>"],[1,8373305,0,0,0,0,"2017-03-11T03:25:40","Shepherdess","",[],"<p>The twat bots are the W O R S T.. Oh yeay I have a new follow.. DAMNIT!!! </p>"],[1,8373551,0,1,0,1,"2017-03-11T03:52:08","Gamio","[e]",[],"<p>I made an account in 2010, was randomly followed by a lot of people (about 50 people) of which maybe 10 were my irl friends and one was someone I knew online. I deleted my account in 2011 but about two weeks after that some sketchy shit started to happen, I got a half dozen &quot;you have registered with Twitter&quot; claiming my personal email address.</p>\n<p>Really fucking shitty nonsense, shit I'm pretty sure that could have happened to anyone registered and deleted their account e.g. Twitter is generating fake accounts to make up for any &quot;lost&quot; accounts.</p>"],[1,8374073,0,1,0,1,"2017-03-11T05:12:29","Grumpy_Old_Man","",[],"<p>I've had a twitter account for about 2 years. I still haven't figured out how it works.</p>"],[2,8375412,8374073,3,0,3,"2017-03-11T09:45:58","dingomeat","[e]",[],"<p>Step 1: create account</p>\n<p>Step 2: subscribe to donald trump</p>\n<p>Step 3: immediately get banned</p>"],[1,8374259,0,0,0,0,"2017-03-11T05:43:56","not_shadowbanned_yet","",[],"<p>and that's not even counting all the thots.</p>"],[1,8374811,0,1,0,1,"2017-03-11T07:22:23","BoraxTheFungarian","",[],"<p>Most of the people on twitter, I wouldn't consider human.</p>"],[1,8374828,0,0,0,0,"2017-03-11T07:26:44","HeavyBeefCurtain","",[],"<p>They are even creating their own hash tags.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Artificially manufacturing something that's supposed to arise from popularity and use</p>\n</blockquote>"],[1,8374872,0,0,0,0,"2017-03-11T07:39:14","Gargilius","",[],"<p>...but but but, what if they <em>identify as</em> people, shouldn't they be treat like people? (trying to keep up with the trends of the days)</p>"],[1,8375035,0,0,0,0,"2017-03-11T08:16:34","Wulfgar","",[],"<p>Twitter is a ad scam.</p>"],[1,8375177,0,0,0,0,"2017-03-11T08:51:58","frankenmine","",[],"<p>NBC/CNBC/MSNBC is corrupt and should be archived in the OP. It doesn't deserve our support. Please keep this in mind for future posts.</p>\n<p>Also, please see:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://voat.co/v/news/comments/1315115\">https://voat.co/v/news/comments/1315115</a></p>"],[1,8375536,0,0,0,0,"2017-03-11T10:35:21","vastrightwing","",[],"<p>Good example of AI technology destroying the economy. AI does not spend money. Twitter has lots of AI accounts posing as people (fake). Twitter advertisers don't want bots clicking on ads and they don't want to pay for bot views. It's like the stock market, bots have replaced people trading stocks. Stock prices now reflect algorithms and not value to people.</p>\n<p>As Twitter advertisers realize they are paying a lot of money for bot clicks and 20% or more active accounts are bots, they will stop advertising. The platform is doomed.</p>\n<p>The stock market is not a place real people should go to buy stocks because it's infested with AI now.</p>"],[1,8377802,0,0,0,0,"2017-03-11T17:05:45","wgtt911","",[],"<p>and there's some questions regarding MOST of those who are...</p>"],[1,8378358,0,0,0,0,"2017-03-11T18:10:44","sampson9","",[],"<p>Actually Bill Clinton's wife only has 13 million followers I think this estimate is too high</p>"],[1,8384574,0,0,0,0,"2017-03-12T07:04:37","Damnpasswords","",[],"<p>Black Twitter is that big?</p>"]]
